{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310681,"nonce":"m9n6IAKSot/+Sck8TAGwEtI4iTk=","title":"Q8_0 KV cache port abandoned 2026-06-05 after two distinct Haxe/JIT issues blocked the implementation. Runtime (alloc + quantise-on-append ...","message":"Goal: cut attention memory bandwidth + KV cache footprint by storing K/V\nas Q8_0 (32-element block: 2-byte f16 scale + 32 i8 quants). Projection\nwas +10-15% wall on long-context decode plus ~3.76× smaller cache.\n\n\nAll runtime + compiler-stdlib + Haxe-extern code was written and\nbuildable. The key pieces:\n\n- `rayzor_kv_cache_q8_alloc(max_seq_len, num_kv_heads, head_dim) -\u003e i64`\n  — malloc + zero-init a raw byte buffer sized for the Q8_0 layout.\n- `rayzor_kv_cache_q8_free(ptr)` — release.\n- `rayzor_kv_cache_q8_append(cache_ptr, max, h, d, current, src_tensor)`\n  — quantise each F32 row on the fly + write Q8_0 bytes.\n- `rayzor_tensor_flash_attn_decode_q8(q, k_cache, v_cache, max, cur,\n  nqh, nkvh, hd, scale) -\u003e Tensor` — fused decode-step kernel that\n  dequants K/V block-by-block into a 32-f32 stack buffer before\n  reusing `dot_slice_f32` / `axpy_slice`.\n- `rayzor_kv_cache_q8_dequant_view(cache_ptr, cur, h, d) -\u003e Tensor`\n  — fresh owning F32 tensor for the prefill bmm path.\n- MIR wrappers `Tensor_kvCacheQ8Alloc` / `Free` / `Append` /\n  `DequantView` / `flashAttnDecodeQ8`.\n- runtime_mapping entries with `params: 3` / `params: 1` / `params: 6`\n  / `params: 4` / `params: 8`.\n- Haxe externs on `rayzor.ds.Tensor` as `static` methods (alloc/free/\n  append/dequantView) and `instance` method (flashAttnDecodeQ8).\n- `nue/transformer/KVCache.hx` with new fields `kQ8Ptr: Int`,\n  `vQ8Ptr: Int`, `useQ8: Bool`; opt-out env var; default-on when\n  `headDim % 32 == 0`.\n- `nue/transformer/GQAttention.hx` flash branch that dispatches to\n  `flashAttnDecodeQ8` when `cache.useQ8` and frees the wasted F32\n  dequant views on success.\n\nThe runtime kernels were spot-checked stand-alone — quant/dequant\nround-trip is the standard Q8_0 layout, math matches llama.cpp's\n`quantize_row_q8_0_ref`.\n\n\n\nCalling `Sys.getEnv(\"RAYZOR_KV_Q8\")` once per `KVCache.new` (16 times\nduring model build) caused decode to hang silently at\n`[gen] streaming...`. With the call removed (hardcoded `canQuant =\nfalse`), the F32 fallback path worked normally.\n\nWorkaround attempts that did NOT help: lazy static-method cache,\nmodule-level `private static var Q8_OPT_OUT_CHECKED:Bool`. Both still\ninvolved Sys.getEnv at some point.\n\nWorkaround that DID help: hardcode the env decision out of the class\ninit body entirely. `Sys.getEnv` used elsewhere (LlamaArch.build for\nthe lm_head re-quant) works fine — once per model build, not once per\nlayer. Smells like a class-init-context-specific JIT issue worsened by\nthe new fields' layout shift (same family as the Linear.hx note about\n`Null\u003cTensor\u003e` field shifting class layout and surfacing latent JIT\nbugs in large import graphs).\n\n\nWith Sys.getEnv removed and Q8 mode forced on, prefill hung in\n`cache.append`. Diagnostic printed `kQ8Ptr=1916796928` (= 0x723A4000),\nwhich is the low 32 bits of a real macOS malloc address. The pointer\nwas correct out of `rayzor_kv_cache_q8_alloc` but got truncated by the\ntime it crossed back into the Haxe heap as `var kp:Int`.\n\nThe lm_head re-quant uses an equivalent pattern (`QTensor`\ni64-pointer-as-Int) and works fine, so the breakage is specific to\neither:\n- the `map_method!(static ...)` mapping for a function returning `I64`\n  to an `Int`-typed Haxe var, or\n- the MIR wrapper losing high bits in `builder.ret(Some(result))` when\n  the body is `let result = builder.call(...).unwrap();`\n\nI didn't dig into the compiler internals; the symptom is what we have.\n\n\nTwo options that avoid both issues:\n\n1. **Opaque extern class wrapping the cache.** Define\n   `rayzor.ds.Q8KvCache` as an `extern class` (like `Tensor` /\n   `QTensor`), so the i64 handle round-trips through the same path that\n   already works for those types. Move alloc/append/dequantView onto\n   the class as instance methods. The static-function-returning-i64\n   path that broke would be sidestepped entirely.\n\n2. **Read env var in `nue.Main` and pass the bool down through the\n   `LlamaArch.build` chain into `KVCache.new` as a constructor arg.**\n   Eliminates Sys.getEnv from class init bodies. Pairs with (1) for\n   cleanliness.\n\nEstimated effort to retry once those two patterns are agreed: ~half\na day. The runtime kernels are correct and reusable — only the Haxe\nwiring needs the alternate approach.\n\n\nNothing. Tree is at 36a2f8b. The runtime quant code (`quantize_q8_0_block`,\n`dequant_q8_0_block`, the four FFI functions) is documented above and\nin the prior commit's diff for later resurrection but is not currently\nin the repo.\n\n\nTried again with the opaque extern class approach to fix the i64 → i32\ntruncation. Made it functionally work on the canonical Paris MATCH, but\nthe user pushed back on architectural placement in three escalating\nrounds:\n\n1. `@:derive([Clone])` hit a hardcoded match arm in `hir_to_mir.rs`\n   that enumerated `rayzor.ds.Tensor` / `rayzor.ds.QTensor` explicitly.\n   **Fixed at commit 7ea611d** — clone extern names are now derived by\n   convention (`rayzor.ds.X` → `rayzor_x_clone`) so any future extern\n   class with `@:derive([Clone])` works without compiler core changes.\n   This is the one durable cleanup from this attempt.\n\n2. `KvCacheQ8.hx` in `compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/ds/` — user: \"KV Cache\n   honestly has no business being an stdlib\". Correct: rayzor stdlib is\n   domain-agnostic numerical primitives; KV cache is transformer-domain.\n\n3. Tried moving to a `nue-plugins` workspace crate registered in\n   `src/main.rs`. User: \"Don't pollute rayzor CLI with downstream\n   elements. Why are you not bundling as rpkg?\". Also correct: rayzor\n   binary should be domain-agnostic; nue should ship as an rpkg\n   package whose native plugin gets dlopen'd via the existing rpkg\n   loader path.\n\n\nThere's no rpkg → native-lib build pipeline today. The infrastructure\n*exists* (`rayzor_plugin::declare_native_methods!` macro for cdylibs,\n`RpkgPlugin` loader, `native_lib_bytes` payload in rpkg files), and\n`rayzor-gpu` uses it. What's missing for nue:\n\n- `BuildConfig` in `compiler/src/workspace/manifest.rs` has no\n  `native-lib` field. To bundle a cdylib alongside Haxe sources, the\n  manifest needs to declare its path so the packer copies it into the\n  rpkg.\n- The packer (`compiler/src/rpkg/pack.rs::add_native_lib`) exists but\n  isn't called from any nue build step.\n- nue would need a `Cargo.toml` for the cdylib, a `declare_native_methods!`\n  invocation listing its extern classes, and a build script that wires\n  the .dylib into the .rpkg.\n\nEstimated to land cleanly: 1 substantive session for the rpkg pipeline,\nthen half a day to re-add the Q8 KV runtime code + Haxe wiring on top.\n\n\nSame as before: do the rpkg-native-lib pipeline work first, then the\nruntime kernels (alloc/quantise-on-append/flash/dequant) drop back\nin 100 LOC each. The runtime code from attempt #2 was correct in\nisolation (Paris MATCH passed when functionally wired); only the\n*placement* was wrong.\n\n- [[perf-flash-attn-decode]] — the F32-cache flash kernel still in use\n- [[bugs-llama-chat-heap-corruption-confirmed]] — same family of\n  \"new fields shift class layout, breaking downstream JIT code\"\n- [[project-optimization-roadmap]] — Q8_0 KV was the next listed lever\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_q8_kv_cache_attempted` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}